# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4-seats8-262k window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/seats8-262k and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Every value is final.
# ORDER.txt says the order, each job's stop rule, its minutes and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-1 is the STAGE-2 image: built by SB9 from the commit
# that records the stage-1 evidence (packed_any_evidence_tp4_262144.json and ordered_writer_evidence_tp4.json at their pins), WITHOUT a baked default: the
# eight-seat 131k image tp4-serve-8 stays what ships until the owner says otherwise. Each job names its profile explicitly. A commit that changes a file the
# image carries needs a new SB9 build and a new tag in every template.
# M9a (STOP, memory): ONE cold 253,920-token prompt on the 262k traffic profile (C2_GATE_MEMORY_USERS=1: the memory plan's concurrent arm is one stream, not eight). It
# measures the prefill's DRAM transient beside the blocks and the engine's, and sets the three DRAM admission bounds
# (QWEN_FAST_DRAM_ENGINE_BUILD_MB / PREFILL_TRANSIENT_MB / LARGEST_BUFFER_MB, whole megabytes in the profile's env: a re-set needs no image rebuild) and whether
# the optional long-prefill tier (QWEN_FAST_DRAM_PREFILL_LONG_FROM / _MB) is worth turning on. READ the [MEMLEDGER] before-points of the prefill: free
# less the stranded bytes less the estimate at least 0.25 GB per chip, and the largest free block less the largest buffer and the prefill's transient at least
# 0.256 GB. Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; attach 15-40 min; one 253,920-token prefill 5-15 min; the short arm 5 min: 30 / 45 / 60 min.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k
C2_GATE_PLAN=memory
C2_GATE_MEMORY_PROMPT=253920
C2_GATE_MEMORY_USERS=1
C2_GATE_JIT=record
